The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (!q->poll_stat)
    return 0;
```
Reason:
This check ensures that the function returns early if `q->poll_stat` is not allocated (i.e., is `NULL`). By doing this, it prevents any further attempts to access `q->poll_stat`, thus avoiding the potential kernel panic caused by dereferencing a `NULL` pointer.

